<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply off $1.2 bln in April 14 wk.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply off $1.2 bln in April 14 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply fell $1.2 billion in the April 14 week to $3,895.8 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $14.4 billion to $5,046.7 billion. M-1 fell $8.9 billion to $1,056.4 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,891.6 billion versus $3,886.9 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
